-- The same two landmarks, withheld at every zoom level.
--
-- The honest version of `hide-landmarks.cql2`, and the one that shows what
-- honesty costs. Overviews are built by averaging the level below, so the
-- pixels over a withheld location are present in every coarser tile too. To
-- actually hide the location you have to withhold those tiles as well -- and
-- one level-5 tile covers the entire image, so the zoomed-out view goes black.
--
-- There is no third option at tile granularity. Either the location is
-- recoverable from the overviews, or the overviews are unusable. Choosing
-- means deciding which of the two you can live with.

region.kind = 'metadata'

OR (region.kind = 'tile'
    AND NOT S_INTERSECTS(region.geom, POLYGON((
      255320 6250770, 255525 6250770, 255525 6250975, 255320 6250975, 255320 6250770)))
    AND NOT S_INTERSECTS(region.geom, POLYGON((
      255350 6253350, 255610 6253350, 255610 6253600, 255350 6253600, 255350 6253350))))
